invariant: INV-14
file: srv_parser.c
catches: srv_quic_test
reason: the frozen digest adds the covered extensions in the order the client
  sent them, which is what the parser did before docs/decisions.md 59. A
  second ClientHello that keeps every extension and moves one then has
  another digest, and srv_check_retry_hello refuses it with
  illegal_parameter. ngtcp2's interop client sends exactly that hello when
  a server asks it for X25519MLKEM768, and RFC 9846 §4.3 lets extensions
  appear in any order (rfc9846.txt:1669-1670). test/srv_quic_retry_tests.h
  replays ngtcp2's two recorded hellos and requires the reordered one to
  complete the handshake.

--- old
    add_frozen_extensions(&p.frozen, exts, exts_len);
--- new
    (void)add_frozen_extensions;
    rbuf wire;
    rb_init(&wire, exts, exts_len);
    while (rb_left(&wire) > 0) {
        const uint8_t *ext = rb_bytes(&wire, 0);
        uint16_t type = rb_u16(&wire);
        size_t len = rb_u16(&wire);
        rb_skip(&wire, len);
        if (frozen_covers(type)) {
            sha256_update(&p.frozen, ext, 4 + len);
        }
    }
